From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:23:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] framebuffer: run due callbacks in time order

framebuffer_schedule put each callback at the front of the list and
schedule_run runs the due ones from the front, so callbacks due in the
same run ran newest first: setTimeout(a, 0); setTimeout(b, 0) ran b
before a whenever the main loop had not polled in between (always under
X, where MutationObserver's delivery timer for the parser's records then
ran after a script's later timer).  The list is now kept in time order,
equal times in the order they were added.
---
 netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/schedule.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/schedule.c b/netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/schedule.c
index 6d17112..2ae4e00 100644
--- a/netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/schedule.c
+++ b/netsurf/frontends/framebuffer/schedule.c
@@ -117,9 +117,16 @@ nserror framebuffer_schedule(int tival, void (*callback)(void *p), void *p)
 	nscb->callback = callback;
 	nscb->p = p;
 
-        /* add to list front */
-        nscb->next = schedule_list;
-        schedule_list = nscb;
+	/* keep the list in time order, after callbacks due at the same time
+	 * (schedule_run runs the due ones from the front: added at the
+	 * front, two timeouts due in the same run ran newest first) */
+	{
+		struct nscallback **pp = &schedule_list;
+		while (*pp != NULL && !timercmp(&(*pp)->tv, &nscb->tv, >))
+			pp = &(*pp)->next;
+		nscb->next = *pp;
+		*pp = nscb;
+	}
 
 	return NSERROR_OK;
 }
